                    {
                        "translation_id": "29915df4-a7ed-4fd8-a9a2-27ce39212e1b",
                        "source_entry_id": "e63a2491-930f-35f1-a92f-184372f01b03",
                        "source_sense_id": "c5be268c-76dc-38bc-8ca3-e1fad7ea398c",
                        "source_sense_description": "bepaald soort zoogdier, Mustela putorius",
                        "target_lang_word": "polecat",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "polecat",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8e5d9309-b615-38c6-8fe8-ddb6bfd34196",
                                        "entry_id": "385678cf-3706-34ba-8572-68841e977ac8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A weasel-like animal of the genus Mustela."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4ff55777-8e94-37f7-a682-e3710192081a",
                                        "entry_id": "385678cf-3706-34ba-8572-68841e977ac8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A weasel-like animal of the genus Mustela.",
                                            "notably, the European polecat, Mustela putorius."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "776a1cf9-04b6-45cd-a65b-abf3746aa4fb",
                                                "sense_id": "4ff55777-8e94-37f7-a682-e3710192081a",
                                                "text": "For a long time the dormouse and polecat had seemed to him overfeeble enemies for his restless valour, even as the granary floor seemed to afford too narrow a field. Every day he read the papers of the previous day in the servants' hall of the houses he visited, and it appeared to him that this war in America, which was hailed as the awakening of the spirit of liberty and justice in the New World, ought to produce a revolution in France."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "598909f0-c5f0-4836-9897-40f3369d018d",
                                                "sense_id": "4ff55777-8e94-37f7-a682-e3710192081a",
                                                "text": "By the little garden pergola open to the winds some fluttered peacocks were blotted nervelessly amid the dripping trees, their heads sunk back beneath their wings: while in the pergola itself, like a fallen storm-cloud, lolled a negress, her levelled, polecat eyes semi-veiled by the nebulous alchemy of the rainbow."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "08e0a3c6-32d7-3678-9611-ae409af474a6",
                                        "entry_id": "385678cf-3706-34ba-8572-68841e977ac8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A skunk."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Appalachia",
                                            "Texas"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "191798cd-5afa-35df-b84a-8abf3c9e5fd8",
                                        "entry_id": "385678cf-3706-34ba-8572-68841e977ac8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tubular device used to support lights on a set."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "efb688b5-65da-4a14-a72b-99bdc6ca3616",
                                                "sense_id": "191798cd-5afa-35df-b84a-8abf3c9e5fd8",
                                                "text": "This is adjustable telescopic tubing, wedged securely between floor and ceiling (vertical pole) or wall-to-wall (horizontal pole), within corridors, arches, window openings, doorways, etc. It may be held in position by a strong internal spring or end-screws. Designs include polecat, varipole, barricuda, jack tube, Acrow."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e6d3500-1ce5-4c79-8da3-7d0d8bffeb11",
                                                "sense_id": "191798cd-5afa-35df-b84a-8abf3c9e5fd8",
                                                "text": "This uses a battery-operated HMI/MSR 200 W rigged on a magic arm fastened to a vertical 'pole-cat'. Check that the car roof is suitable for this application and remember to include a clean card (beer mat) between the top of the pole-cat and the car roof!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "672e7d85-e21e-4bda-897f-281fe3519aa7",
                        "source_entry_id": "e63a2491-930f-35f1-a92f-184372f01b03",
                        "source_sense_id": "c5be268c-76dc-38bc-8ca3-e1fad7ea398c",
                        "source_sense_description": "bepaald soort zoogdier, Mustela putorius",
                        "target_lang_word": "putois",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "putois",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "341d8dc8-b9e9-31a4-af94-2977a97fc1dc",
                                        "entry_id": "13a4d31f-078d-3f11-a5d1-0d3a197475a6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Petit quadrupède carnivore dont la peau sert à faire des fourrures, possédant une glande libérant une puanteur en cas de peur."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65ff337b-f838-435d-9531-388da74e659f",
                                                "sense_id": "341d8dc8-b9e9-31a4-af94-2977a97fc1dc",
                                                "text": "Je suis ainsi que la bestiole, sur laquelle s’est jeté le putois ; j’ai beau me rouler sur le sol, me débattre désespérément pour échapper à ses crocs, le putois me tient, et il ne me lâche pas…"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b4cc696d-89dd-3c5c-82f9-aebed20e8612",
                                        "entry_id": "13a4d31f-078d-3f11-a5d1-0d3a197475a6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personnage malfaisant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "offensive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49e7f22a-0828-4679-a044-bc36a8ffec3a",
                                                "sense_id": "b4cc696d-89dd-3c5c-82f9-aebed20e8612",
                                                "text": "Ah ! il y en avait des putois en ce monde et des putasses de putains. Sang de Dieu ! des charognards et des carognes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9470fa41-e656-310a-8d9e-7e652f8a5640",
                                        "entry_id": "13a4d31f-078d-3f11-a5d1-0d3a197475a6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pinceau à poils courts utilisé par les céramistes, généralement ce pinceau est en poil de putois."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2047d30c-b15e-4c72-999f-6baac38d9e53",
                                                "sense_id": "9470fa41-e656-310a-8d9e-7e652f8a5640",
                                                "text": "Les dégradés et nuagés étaient obtenus lorsqu'on passait la couleur avec une queue de morue puis en tamponnant avec un putois pour finir de l'appliquer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
